ort\"], \"scope\": \"Recorded fixed benchmark or explicitly conditional source-based specification; no causal component attribution\"}\n{\"claim\": \"Stanford3 Strong linear seed-mean exposure support: {\\\"fraction_one\\\": 0.03205736808792221, \\\"fraction_zero\\\": 0.03242059382012774, \\\"linear_design_condition\\\": 9.193799507457536, \\\"maximum\\\": 1.0, \\\"minimum\\\": 0.0}\", \"source_ids\": [\"final.evidence.episodes\"], \"citation_keys\": [], \"evidence_refs\": [\"analysis/summary.json#/support\"], \"scope\": \"Recorded fixed benchmark or explicitly conditional source-based specification; no causal component attribution\"}\n{\"claim\": \"Stanford3 Cluster seed-mean exposure support: {\\\"fraction_one\\\": 0.03979299729558663, \\\"fraction_zero\\\": 0.04890960354450774, \\\"linear_design_condition\\\": 7.208791238224571, \\\"maximum\\\": 1.0, \\\"minimum\\\": 0.0}\", \"source_ids\": [\"final.evidence.episodes\"], \"citation_keys\": [], \"evidence_refs\": [\"analysis/summary.json#/support\"], \"scope\": \"Recorded fixed benchmark or explicitly conditional source-based specification; no causal component attribution\"}\n{\"claim\": \"Ratio plots divide cell RMSEs and bootstrap complete seed blocks. The resampling uses 10000 draws, seed 20261107, and 95% percentile intervals. Intervals quantify fixed-benchmark Monte Carlo variation, not causal coverage or graph-population generalization.\", \"source_ids\": [\"final.evidence.episodes\"], \"citation_keys\": [], \"evidence_refs\": [\"analysis/summary.json#/bootstrap\", \"build_paper_artifacts.py\"], \"scope\": \"Recorded fixed benchmark or explicitly conditional source-based specification; no causal component attribution\"}\n{\"claim\": \"The benchmark uses 4096-node synthetic SBM, BA and WS graphs, and fixed Stanford3 with 11586 nodes and 568309 undirected edges. SBM uses four blocks with probabilities .04/.002; BA attachment is five; WS neighborhood is ten with rewiring .15. Covariates have one column. Synthetic topologies vary by seed and Stanford3 topology does not.\", \"source_ids\": [\"final.evidence.episodes\"], \"citation_keys\": [], \"evidence_refs\": [\"source_evidence/benchmark_manifest.json#/generator\", \"source_evidence/benchmark_manifest.json#/records\", \"reproducibility/resources/final/benchmark.npz\"], \"scope\": \"Recorded fixed benchmark or explicitly conditional source-based specification; no causal component attribution\"}\n{\"claim\": \"The outcome model is .5*x + z + spillover + unit Gaussian noise. Six spillovers are 0, .25*e, 2*e, 2*I(e>=.75)+z*e, 2*h, and 2*e under cluster assignment. Recorded GATEs are respectively 1, 1.25, 3, 4, 3, 3. Two-hop exposure includes backtracking; isolates have zero exposure.\", \"source_ids\": [\"final.evidence.episodes\"], \"citation_keys\": [], \"evidence_refs\": [\"source_evidence/evaluate_final.py#L676-L694\", \"source_evidence/benchmark_manifest.json#/mechanisms\", \"paper_data.json#/final_evaluation/evaluation_evidence/episodes\"], \"scope\": \"Recorded fixed benchmark or explicitly conditional source-based specification; no causal component attribution\"}\n{\"claim\": \"Individual assignment is Bernoulli(.5). The cluster design uses 32 deterministic balanced graph-BFS clusters and independent Bernoulli(.5) cluster assignment; it changes the joint assignment distribution rather than exposure support alone.\", \"source_ids\": [\"final.evidence.episodes\"], \"citation_keys\": [], \"evidence_refs\": [\"source_evidence/benchmark_manifest.json#/mechanisms\"], \"scope\": \"Recorded fixed benchmark or explicitly conditional source-based specification; no causal component attribution\"}\n{\"claim\": \"The inspected associated estimator has quadratic one-hop features, saved observed-data standardization, SVD, endpoint-contrast risk grid n*{0,1e-6,1e-4,1e-2,1}, and deterministic minimum selection. Source association is not an independently reconstructed executable-identity proof.\", \"source_ids\": [\"result.best_correct_score\", \"final.evidence.episodes\"], \"citation_keys\": [], \"evidence_refs\": [\"source_evidence/estimator.py#L83-L160\", \"source_evidence/program_spec.toml\"], \"scope\": \"Recorded fixed benchmark or explicitly conditional source-based specification; no causal component attribution\"}\n{\"claim\": \"The fixed-penalty risk expression equals squared bias plus contrast variance only under the stated correct-reference and noise assumptions. The selected minimum is not an unbiased selected-risk estimate; empirical calibration is unmeasured.\", \"source_ids\": [\"result.best_correct_score\"], \"citation_keys\": [\"Stein1981\", \"Efron1986\"], \"evidence_refs\": [\"source_evidence/estimator.py#L127-L151\"], \"scope\": \"Recorded fixed benchmark or explicitly conditional source-based specification; no causal component attribution\"}\n{\"claim\": \"Rank tolerance is max(design shape)*machine epsilon*smax, contrast residual tolerance 1e-8*max(1,norm(q)), residual df n-r-1. The fallback uses hinges .25,.5,.75, ridge 1e-3, and unpenalized intercept. Exact-constant outcomes have zero contrast. Fallback and penalty frequencies are unavailable.\", \"source_ids\": [\"result.best_correct_score\"], \"citation_keys\": [], \"evidence_refs\": [\"source_evidence/estimator.py#L69-L81\", \"source_evidence/estimator.py#L119-L158\", \"source_evidence/estimator.py#L199-L213\"], \"scope\": \"Recorded fixed benchmark or explicitly conditional source-based specification; no causal component attribution\"}\n{\"claim\": \"The three substantive comparators are difference in means, covariate-adjusted own-treatment OLS and linear one-hop OLS, evaluated on matched cases. OLS endpoint contrast accounts for nonisolated-node fraction.\", \"source_ids\": [\"final.evidence.episodes\"], \"citation_keys\": [], \"evidence_refs\": [\"source_evidence/evaluate_final.py#L371-L392\"], \"scope\": \"Recorded fixed benchmark or explicitly conditional source-based specification; no causal component attribution\"}\n{\"claim\": \"Component ablations, same-reference GCV comparison, original-hinge matched final comparison, inference coverage, risk calibration and additional noise studies are absent; missing measurements do not establish inferior performance.\", \"source_ids\": [\"final.evidence.episodes\"], \"citation_keys\": [], \"evidence_refs\": [\"paper_data.json#/ablation_studies\", \"paper_data.json#/final_evaluation/evaluation_evidence/episodes\"], \"scope\": \"Recorded fixed benchmark or explicitly conditional source-based specification; no causal component attribution\"}\n{\"claim\": \"Recorded control success is 1 and failed-episode fraction 0. Qualification and limited behavioral controls do not establish arbitrary-interference validity; candidate internal diagnostics are unverified.\", \"source_ids\": [\"final.metric.control_success_fraction\", \"final.metric.failed_episode_fraction\", \"final.qualification.outcome\"], \"citation_keys\": [], \"evidence_refs\": [\"paper_data.json#/final_evaluation/metrics\", \"paper_data.json#/final_evaluation/evaluation_evidence/candidate_diagnostics_trust\"], \"scope\": \"Recorded fixed benchmark or explicitly conditional source-based specification; no causal component attribution\"}\n{\"claim\": \"The evaluator caps signed errors at magnitude 10 and normalizes by unit noise; it averages cell RMSEs and absolute biases equally, not pooled squared errors.\", \"source_ids\": [\"final.metric.mean_capped_normalized_rmse\", \"final.metric.mean_absolute_capped_normalized_bias\", \"final.evidence.episodes\"], \"citation_keys\": [], \"evidence_refs\": [\"source_evidence/benchmark_manifest.json#/aggregation\", \"analysis/summary.json\"], \"scope\": \"Recorded fixed benchmark or explicitly conditional source-based specification; no causal component attribution\"}\n{\"claim\": \"Reproduction uses archived PCG64-generated inputs, seed+100003*(family ordinal+1), the listed 24 seeds, declared NumPy1.26.4/SciPy1.13.1/NetworkX3.3, two CPU cores a